      "line_end": 12,
      "title": "Request query string passed to eval",
      "description": "The /calc handler passes req.query.expr straight to eval. The added suppression comments hide this from the linters. Any caller of /calc can run arbitrary JavaScript inside the server process. That gives them full remote code execution. Remove eval and parse the expression with a restricted arithmetic evaluator. Reject any input that is not numbers and operators.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:openqodex.suppression-added",
      "candidate": "c5",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The /calc handler passes req.query.expr straight to eval. The added suppression comments hide this from the linters.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of /calc can run arbitrary JavaScript inside the server process. That gives them full remote code execution.",
      "fix": "Remove eval and parse the expression with a restricted arithmetic evaluator. Reject any input that is not numbers and operators."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "security",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "tools/thumbs.py",
      "line_number": 9,
      "line_end": 9,
      "title": "Upload name interpolated into a shell command",
      "description": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name, which comes from the upload form, into a command string. subprocess.run then runs that string through a shell. An uploader can choose a name with shell metacharacters and run commands on the host. A name with dot-dot segments can also read or write files outside the upload folders. Pass an argument list without shell=True. Reduce upload_name to its basename and reject names with path separators.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
      "source": "semgrep:python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name, which comes from the upload form, into a command string. subprocess.run then runs that string through a shell.",
      "consequence": "An uploader can choose a name with shell metacharacters and run commands on the host. A name with dot-dot segments can also read or write files outside the upload folders.",
      "fix": "Pass an argument list without shell=True. Reduce upload_name to its basename and reject names with path separators."
    },
